  "final_message": "The link bookmarking app is built, but I never built or ran the Docker image. I also never tested the frontend in a browser, though `npm run build` and the TypeScript check pass.\n\nI tested the API directly in Flask's test client and under gunicorn. That covered:\n- registration and login;\n- creating, listing, refreshing and deleting previews;\n- another user's preview returning 404;\n- paging and its validation;\n- the health endpoint;\n- the built frontend being served at `/`.\n\n- **Backend:** `app.py` has the routes, and `db.py`, `fetcher.py` and `extract.py` hold the SQLite setup, page fetching and metadata extraction. Data goes in `./data/app.db`.\n- **Plain text:** Titles and descriptions are stored as plain text. Markup is not interpreted on the server, and React escapes it when it renders.\n- **Fetching:** Redirects are followed up to 5 times. The response is capped at 1 MB and the whole fetch at 15 seconds. Only `http` and `https` links work. Redirects are checked as well, so a link can't redirect to a blocked address.\n- **Blocked addresses:** Link-local addresses such as `169.254.169.254` and unspecified addresses such as `0.0.0.0` are rejected. Loopback and private-range addresses are allowed by default. Setting `BLOCK_PRIVATE_FETCH=1` blocks those too. I left them open because the sandbox probably only has local targets to test against.\n- **Frontend:** React with Tailwind in `frontend/src/` (`App.tsx`, `AuthForm.tsx`, `PreviewCard.tsx`, `api.ts`). It has the sign-in and register form, the username with a sign-out button, the Add field with a loading state, and preview cards with refresh, delete and paging.\n- **Extras and config:** I added `GET /api/me` and `POST /api/auth/logout`, which the frontend uses. Sessions last 7 days. I added a `.gitignore` and gave gunicorn 2 workers with 8 threads each in the `Dockerfile`.\n- **Dependencies:** I added Tailwind, TypeScript and the React type packages to the frontend. `backend/requirements.txt` is unchanged.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
